        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: G. D. Spradlin, Marlon Brando, Soo Yong\n- Works: Sayonara, On the Waterfront, The Godfather, A Streetcar Named Desire, Viva Zapata!, The Good Earth, Love Is a Many-Splendored Thing\n- Topics: film and television acting credits\n\nFacts:\n- Soo Yong appeared in the films The Good Earth (1937), Love Is a Many-Splendored Thing (1955), and Sayonara (1957).\n- Sayonara is a 1957 Technicolor American film starring Marlon Brando in Technirama.\n- Marlon Brando is widely known for Academy Award-winning performances as Terry Malloy in On the Waterfront (1954) and Vito Corleone in The Godfather (1972).\n- Marlon Brando is also known for performances in A Streetcar Named Desire (1951) and Viva Zapata!.\n- G. D. Spradlin is credited in over 70 television and film productions.\n- G. D. Spradlin performed alongside actors including Marlon Brando, Al Pacino, Charlton Heston, George C. Scott, and Johnny Depp.",
